---
import { methods, phases, resource, solves, title } from '@/data/fingr'
import Analytics from '@vercel/analytics/astro'
import SpeedInsights from '@vercel/speed-insights/astro'

import AnalyticsScripts from '@/components/AnalyticsScripts.astro'
import BaseHead from '@/components/BaseHead.astro'
import ThemeProvider from '@/components/layout/ThemeProvider.astro'
import FingrPipeline from '@/components/projects/FingrPipeline.astro'

import '@/assets/styles/app.css'
import '@/assets/styles/fingr.css'

const links = [
  { label: 'Paper', icon: '/icons/project.svg#mingcute-document-3-line' },
  {
    label: 'Video',
    icon: '/icons/project.svg#mingcute-video-2-line',
    href: 'https://youtu.be/Sw45m8cqYPo'
  },
  { label: 'X Post', icon: '/icons/social.svg#mingcute-x-line' },
  {
    label: 'Visualization',
    icon: '/icons/project.svg#mingcute-package-2-line',
    href: '#visualization'
  },
  { label: 'BibTeX', icon: '/icons/project.svg#mingcute-document-3-line', href: '#bibtex' }
]

const bibtex = `@article{fingr2026,
  title={FINGR: Learning Dexterous Hand Control for Real-World Rubik's Cube Solving},
  author={Anonymous},
  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:XXXX.XXXXX},
  year={2026}
}`
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang='en'>
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title={title}
      description='Finger-relative geometry and future interaction prediction for real-world Rubik’s Cube solving.'
      canonical='/projects/FINGR'
      ogImage={resource('media/real-setup.webp')}
      lang='en'
    />
    <ThemeProvider />
    <AnalyticsScripts />
  </head>
  <body class='fingr-page'>
    <main id='fingr'>
      <header class='project-header'>
        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <nav class='resource-links' aria-label='Project resources'>
          {
            links.map((link) =>
              link.href ? (
                <a href={link.href}>
                  <svg aria-hidden='true'>
                    <use href={link.icon} />
                  </svg>
                  {link.label}
                </a>
              ) : (
                <button type='button' aria-disabled='true' title={`${link.label} — coming soon`}>
                  <svg aria-hidden='true'>
                    <use href={link.icon} />
                  </svg>
                  {link.label}
                  <span class='sr-only'> — coming soon</span>
                </button>
              )
            )
          }
        </nav>
      </header>

      <section id='video'>
        <h2>Video</h2>
        <video
          class='main-video'
          data-src={resource('media/fingr.mp4')}
          poster={resource('media/fingr.webp')}
          controls
          playsinline
          preload='none'
          aria-label='FINGR video'></video>
      </section>

      <section id='abstract'>
        <h2>Abstract</h2>
        <p>
          Manipulating a Rubik's Cube with one single dexterous hand is a challenging test of
          sustained, contact-rich control: the hand must execute successive layer turns while
          keeping the cube secure. Each turn requires some fingers to support the cube while others
          push a moving layer, release contact, and reset for the next move. To learn this
          coordination, we introduce <strong>FINGR</strong> (Future-supervised Interaction Network with
          Geometric Representations), a policy that combines finger-relative geometry with future interaction
          prediction. A shared point encoder expresses the cube relative to each fingertip and aggregates
          its points without depending on cubie indexing. Learned future tokens share the observation
          encoder and receive supervision for contact-force changes, layer-turn progress, and finger joint
          displacement at multiple time scales. The resulting representation conditions a flow policy
          that directly generates finger actions. On a real dexterous hand, our policy achieves around
          {' '}<strong>99.0%</strong>{' '}
          success over 300 turn attempts, compared with <strong>79.7%</strong> for the base flow policy.
          Integrated with grasping and table-assisted regrasping, the policy solves all ten scrambled
          2×2×2 cubes in a mean complete-system time of approximately <strong>137 seconds</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id='method'>
        <h2>Method</h2>
        <a
          class='pipeline-figure'
          href={resource('media/pipeline.svg')}
          target='_blank'
          rel='noreferrer'
          aria-label='Open the full-size method figure'
        >
          <FingrPipeline />
        </a>
        <p class='figure-caption'>
          Finger-relative geometry describes the cube from each fingertip. Predicting future
          contact, turn progress, and finger motion shapes the representation used by the flow
          policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id='experiment'>
        <h2>Experiment</h2>
        <h3>Real Robot Setup</h3>
        <video
          class='real-video'
          data-src={resource('media/real-setup.mp4')}
          poster={resource('media/real-setup.webp')}
          controls
          playsinline
          preload='none'
          aria-label='Real robot pickup and in-hand Rubik’s Cube manipulation, original speed'
        ></video>

        <h3 id='visualization' class='replay-heading'>Complete Solves Trajectory Visualization</h3>
        <div class='replay-selector' aria-label='Choose a scramble'>
          {
            solves.map((solve, i) => (
              <button
                type='button'
                data-solve={i}
                aria-pressed={i === 0}
                aria-label={`Scramble ${i + 1}: ${solve.scramble}`}
              >
                {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
              </button>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <div class='scramble-line'>
          <span>Scramble</span><code id='scramble'>{solves[0].scramble}</code>
        </div>
        <div class='replay-player'>
          <div class='replay-shell'>
            <div id='rerun-root'></div>
            <div id='replay-cover'>
              <button type='button' id='load-replay'>Load Trajectory Visualization</button>
              <p id='replay-status' role='status'></p>
              <progress id='replay-progress' hidden></progress>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class='replay-timeline'>
            <div class='timeline-top'>
              <button type='button' id='replay-play' disabled>Play</button><span id='replay-phase'
                >Ready to explore</span
              ><output id='replay-clock'>0:00 / 0:00</output>
            </div>
            <div class='timeline-track'>
              <div id='phase-track' aria-label='Replay phases'></div>
              <div id='move-markers' aria-hidden='true'></div>
              <label
                ><span class='sr-only'>Replay time</span><input
                  id='replay-time'
                  type='range'
                  min='0'
                  max='1'
                  value='0'
                  step='0.01'
                  disabled
                /></label
              >
            </div>
            <div class='phase-legend'>
              {
                phases.map((p) => (
                  <span>
                    <i class={`phase-${p.key}`} />
                    {p.label}
                  </span>
                ))
              }
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class='execution'>
            <span class='execution-label'>Execution</span><div
              id='replay-moves'
              aria-label='Executed moves and recovery steps'
            >
            </div>
          </div>
          <label class='replay-forces'
            ><input type='checkbox' id='show-forces' disabled />Contact Forces</label
          >
          <p class='replay-feedback' id='replay-feedback' role='status'></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id='results'>
        <h2>Results</h2>
        <h3>Layer-turn Success</h3>
        <div class='result-controls'>
          <div class='segmented' aria-label='Comparison'>
            <button type='button' data-comparison='baselines' aria-pressed='true'>Baselines</button
            ><button type='button' data-comparison='ablation' aria-pressed='false'>Ablation</button>
          </div>
          <div class='segmented' aria-label='Turn direction'>
            <button type='button' data-metric='overall' aria-pressed='true'>Overall</button><button
              type='button'
              data-metric='u'
              aria-pressed='false'>U</button
            ><button type='button' data-metric='l' aria-pressed='false'>L</button>
          </div>
          <span id='attempt-count'>300 attempts / method</span>
        </div>
        <div class='result-chart'>
          {
            methods.map((method, i) => (
              <button
                type='button'
                class:list={['result-row', { ours: i === 4 }]}
                data-result={i}
                hidden={i === 3}
                aria-describedby='result-detail'
              >
                <>
                  <span class='method-name'>{method.name}</span>
                  <span class='bar-track'>
                    <span class='bar-fill' style={`width:${method.overall}%`} />
                  </span>
                  <strong>{method.overall.toFixed(1)}%</strong>
                </>
              </button>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <p id='result-detail' class='result-detail' aria-live='polite'>
          FINGR · 99.0% success · 5.25 s per attempt
        </p>

        <h3>Complete Solves</h3>
        <div class='phase-legend'>
          {
            phases.map((p) => (
              <span>
                <i class={`phase-${p.key}`} />
                {p.label}
              </span>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <div class='solve-chart' aria-label='Complete solve time by component, in seconds'>
          <div class='time-axis'>
            <span>0</span><span>50</span><span>100</span><span>150</span><span>200 s</span>
          </div>
          {
            solves.map((solve, i) => (
              <button
                type='button'
                class='solve-row'
                data-timing={i}
                aria-pressed={i === 0}
                aria-describedby='timing-detail'
                aria-label={`Solve ${i + 1}, ${solve.seconds.toFixed(2)} seconds. ${phases.map((p) => `${p.label}: ${solve.timings[p.key].toFixed(2)} seconds`).join('. ')}`}
              >
                <>
                  <span class='solve-number'>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                  <span class='stacked-track'>
                    {phases.map((p) => (
                      <span
                        class={`phase-${p.key}`}
                        style={`width:${solve.timings[p.key] / 2}%`}
                        title={`${p.label}: ${solve.timings[p.key].toFixed(2)} s`}
                      />
                    ))}
                  </span>
                  <strong>{solve.seconds.toFixed(2)} s</strong>
                </>
              </button>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <div id='timing-detail' aria-live='polite'>
          <div class='timing-heading'>
            <strong id='timing-title'>Solve 01 · {solves[0].seconds.toFixed(2)} s</strong>
          </div>
          <dl>
            {
              phases.map((p) => (
                <div>
                  <>
                    <dt>
                      <i class={`phase-${p.key}`} />
                      {p.label}
                    </dt>
                    <dd data-time-component={p.key}>{solves[0].timings[p.key].toFixed(2)} s</dd>
                  </>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id='bibtex'>
        <h2>BibTeX</h2>
        <pre><code>{bibtex}</code></pre>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script>
      import { initFingr } from '../../scripts/fingr'

      document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initFingr)
    </script>
    <Analytics />
    <SpeedInsights />
  </body>
</html>
